{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554315-logistics-of-small-cities","id":1554315,"title":"Logistics of Small Cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-12T05:24:17-07:00","id":1554315,"title":"Logistics of Small Cities","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> I like to think about how my local cities may support a Kindred population, and other ways of connecting VtM to my actual life. However, as a New Englander, the biggest city in my state has a population of just over 100k, which according to the (conservative) rule of thumb, is enough people to support 1 Kindred. The <i>Dark Colony</i> sourcebook further supports this idea by listing the estimated Kindred population via state, with the smaller states (NH, VT, RI) having kindred populations ~12 total.<br /> <br /> Taking the 100k estimate at face value, this would track, but what I'm wondering is exactly, how this might work? Would each Kindred just find themselves princes of empty (of kindred) cities? And would any new Kindred in the domain be turned away automatically, out of fear of overpopulation? Is there any location guides that cover this sort of question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","name":"Matter911","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T05:51:28-07:00","id":1554316,"title":"","content":"To be honest I tend to just ignore that 100K thing<br /> Realistically you have usually in a game a coterie of at least 3 players, so that automatically puts you above the &quot;limit&quot; - and you not even touched the Kidnred bureaucratic system eg. Prince, S\u00e9n\u00e9chal, at least one Scourge (but 3 is prefered), the Sheriff, the Keeper of Elysium, a Harpy (again Harpies prefered, again 3 at least), the Primogens... and the Subjects<br /> <br /> And you not even touched the Independents like Giovanni or Followers of Set, the Anarchs hanging around or the Sabbat spies (or full blown packs), guests, diplomats, etc etc etc<br /> <br /> ...and the occasional ancient vampire sleeping or working behind the scenes<br /> <br /> Soo... yeah, even the 10K sometimes is not enough to have a fully functioning city where there is a reason to, you know, play and have a story<br /> <br /> The best way to handle this to factor in the Herd<br /> Vampires are... lazy, while Hunting is fun for some, i nreality most of the Vampires I think not really go out every night to Hunt<br /> Especially if you are Ventrue with the preference of albanian midget sumo werstlers <br /> Herd, most of the vampires probably have Herds, their neat little food source - be it humans or even acces to a blood bank or keeping kidnapped people in the basement on life support - to lessen the burden on the City<br /> <br /> A Cainite needs one blood/night just to work and lets say they don't use their powers that require vitae, sometimes they have to train, learn, feed their ghouls ,etc. <br /> So having 3-5 ppl Herd? Actually VERY realistic + the occasional hunt and rat-meals if you are a nosferatu or Gangrel<br /> <br /> 100K could support a fully functioning, armed and dangerous Camarilla citiy of 30-40 vampires + the players and enemies without problems in my humble oppinion, and if you want to focus on the food shortage it even presents a neat opportunity how the Prince want to solve things (or task the Palyers to solve this)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T07:31:00-07:00","id":1554317,"title":"","content":"The 100K thing is meant to avoid the vampire population exploding into them fighting with armies and other ridiculousness. Which obviously failed miserably.<br /> <br /> But generally, the argument needs the following to be kept in mind:<br /> <br /> * There's enough food for vampires to live but is there enough that they don't get <i>discovered</i>?<br /> <br /> One really good game is the text based adventure, OUT FOR BLOOD where there's a town of about 10,000 people and a vampire. A 13th generation Toreador and later some Thin Bloods. The single vampire causes the town to massively change and rumors to coalesce around her because her presence is too big to not be noticed as is the occasional accidental deaths that happen. So it turns into the Lost Boys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T09:06:57-07:00","id":1554318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554315-logistics-of-small-cities#post1554315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> I like to think about how my local cities may support a Kindred population, and other ways of connecting VtM to my actual life. However, as a New Englander, the biggest city in my state has a population of just over 100k, which according to the (conservative) rule of thumb, is enough people to support 1 Kindred. The <i>Dark Colony</i> sourcebook further supports this idea by listing the estimated Kindred population via state, with the smaller states (NH, VT, RI) having kindred populations ~12 total.</div> </div> </div> </div>We talked about some of this in one of the threads specifically about New England/Dark Colony. It's a long thread and talks about a lot of other things in that setting, but you may find it useful for those things that are relevant.<br /> <br /> Also, it's important to remember that what is used is not the city's population, but the metropolitan area's population. While technically the Kindred don't usually hunt in the suburbs (because most bedroom communities are not conducive to anonymous hunting/feeding), the people there frequently commute to the city for jobs and night time entertainment so Kindred can indeed feed on them in safer environs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554315-logistics-of-small-cities#post1554315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the 100k estimate at face value, this would track, but what I'm wondering is exactly, how this might work? Would each Kindred just find themselves princes of empty (of kindred) cities? And would any new Kindred in the domain be turned away automatically, out of fear of overpopulation? Is there any location guides that cover this sort of question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is how I would handle it.<br /> <br /> 1) Not all &quot;Princes&quot; are equal. A Prince of a large domain would be more prestigious than a Prince of a very small one. Despite both being termed &quot;Prince&quot; (in the sense that both hold domain in their respective locations, and thus enforce/interpret the Traditions there). In terms of game mechanics, this is probably determined by the Status background. A &quot;true&quot; Prince would have Status 5, while lesser Princes would have Status of only 4 or perhaps even 3, all other things being equal. In <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">False Epiphany</a> chronicle of New Orleans (Blood &amp; Bourbon), he uses the term &quot;couch prince&quot; to distinguish those &quot;princes&quot; of small domains where the entire Kindred population could meet on the couch of the living room of the Prince's house.<br /> <br /> Of course, how many people are in your domain is only one determination. If the Kindred who rules a domain of only 2-3 vampires is also a very old, powerful vampire who could easily claim praxis in a much larger domain, but for her own reasons prefers the isolation and dealing with fewer of her own kind, her Status might be 5 or even higher.<br /> <br /> 2) Some smaller domains may essentially be vassals of one of the larger domains. They are more like a feudal vassal than a prince in their own right. Dark Colony even has that in terms of Prince Quention King and the Six Knights who rule some of the nearby cities that exist outside the immediate Boston metro area (like Worcester). And of course Prince Mithras did the same in Britain, once holding the entire realm of England as his domain. I've seen various titles used by STs for such offices - Dukes, Regents, Castellans, Stewards.<br /> <br /> 3) Similarly there may be domains that are simply held by one vampire or that vampire's small brood. Technically it's a domain, but holding dominion only over yourself or your childe usually isn't what one thinks of when one hears the term Prince. In that New England thread I mentioned earlier, one of the things we discussed was a Dark Shadows type situation with a Barnabas Collins holding &quot;domain&quot; in the fictional Collinsport. One person suggested the term &quot;Squire&quot; be used as a courtesy title to acknowledge he holds domain in terms of the Traditions, but isn't really part of the local political system.<br /> <br /> 4) In terms of larger political confederations in relatively nearby domains, it's probably a Conclave that settles things. We have two examples of such. The first is Chicago where we have two Princes - Lodin and Modius - in the same metropolitan area (Gary, IN is so closely linked to Chicago in real life it is the only part of Indiana which uses the Central Time Zone of Chicago instead of the Eastern Time Zone). In order to curb the ongoing feud, Lodin asked for a Conclave and the resulting vote said a) Modius could call himself Prince, but b) Modius must &quot;confer&quot; with Lodin on anything major that would affect both cities and must essentially abide by Lodin's decisions. Lodin himself sees himself as having absolute control over Gary. The one thing Modius seems to be able to do is approve of Kindred who want to sire new childer.<br /> <br /> Similarly in Dark Colony, we're told of an attempt by the Ventrue (the Wingate Initiative) to create a regional Primogen Council of New England (called Congress) to advise the individual Princes collectively. It didn't really work, but there's no reason why a stronger Primogen Council couldn't have dominated weaker Princes, or such a conclave to establish a single Prince over the entire region. It all depends on what you, the ST, wants to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T09:11:46-07:00","id":1554319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554315-logistics-of-small-cities?p=1554317#post1554317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's enough food for vampires to live but is there enough that they don't get <i>discovered</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye<br /> Technically this is the main question, tho' I would add:<br /> <br /> &quot;Could a vampire kill around one person per month (Frenzy, accident, etc) without drawing attention to the area where she lives in?&quot;<br /> Someone, somewhere WILL fuck up, eventually. It's inevitable.<br /> But <i>not a problem</i> untill the deed starts to attract attention and humans and hunters and other things if you want starting to put one and one together. Not every night ends up with a a blood-drained corpse...<br /> At the end of the day it is all about statictics<br /> These days blending in isn't that hard, there are all kinds of wheirdos living in cities without anyone really noticing them or even if they do they just shrug and move on - pair this with a nice contacts in the Police/Coroner/Press etc, to bury suspicious deaths and disappearances and suddenly you have a very wide wriggling space<br /> <br /> <br /> You can always take the average number of people who disappear in a given year as a starting point to know what is the &quot;line&quot; you don't want to crosss without raising alarms among the authorities<br /> Each year in the United States, more than 600,000 people are reported missing.<br /> That\u2019s more than the population of Vermont.<br /> Roughly 180,000 people go missing in the UK every year<br /> The highest rate of missing persons by far is in sparsely populated Alaska, with 163.76 missing people per 100,000 of the population\u2014 far beyond any other state. The state with the lowest rate of missing persons is Massachusetts, at 2.32 missing persons per 100,000\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> But the number game aside, the key is to handle those suspicious deaths and disappearances your Vampires may cause and while eventually everyone have blood on their hands Vampires try to avoid problems - or have a way to mitigate the consequences<br /> It is not about the lack of food - with a decent Herd as I said it is easy to avoid any problems - but the potential fuck ups the Vampires have to bury after themselves and others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T08:05:20-07:00","id":1554375,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth considering that small-time Vampires are likely to move around a lot in the course of their afterlives - especially in regions with fairly scattered populations - the better to be ignored by dangerous rivals or potential Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T02:55:04-07:00","id":1554407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matter911</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554315-logistics-of-small-cities#post1554315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the 100k estimate at face value, this would track, but what I'm wondering is exactly, how this might work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Practically speaking, you should consider the dynamics of the area.<br /> <br /> If people move a lot, vampires will probably congregate at hubs, places where a lot of people will pass by during the night. Outsiders should also be considered, you're not required by law to take blood only from natives.<br /> <br /> Vampires can also move. A Kindred living in an area with several small towns may travel between them regularly. They may stay only a few nights in each then move, or even just move around and go back home at the end of the night, depending on travel times in the area.<br /> <br /> You'll mostly work with this, but dealing with such areas you should also be more open to unconventional arrangements. A vampire can get along with less mortals if the risk of exposure is diminished somehow, and one way of doing that is actually being open with a small community, so they know they have a predator among them, but also that they can't do anything about it.<br /> <br /> Try to be creative, put yourself in the shoes of a vampire and find out how you can arrange things so you can live in this situation. For bureaucracy, think of what the locals feel they need, based on their relations and ease of locomotion. A powerful Elder may be able to claim Domain over several settlements and any vampire within, nearby vampires may be treated as &quot;vassal princes&quot;, maybe there are no bureaucracy at all, or maybe half of the state works as a single domain with every role filled by someone, somewhere.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately we didn't got many books talking about areas of small communities even if they're still where a lot of people live. In fact, most people in the US do not live in big cities at all. But the books are heavily geared towards metropolitan life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554315-logistics-of-small-cities?p=1554316#post1554316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realistically you have usually in a game a coterie of at least 3 players, so that automatically puts you above the &quot;limit&quot; - and you not even touched the Kidnred bureaucratic system eg. Prince, S\u00e9n\u00e9chal, at least one Scourge (but 3 is prefered), the Sheriff, the Keeper of Elysium, a Harpy (again Harpies prefered, again 3 at least), the Primogens... and the Subjects<br /> <br /> And you not even touched the Independents like Giovanni or Followers of Set, the Anarchs hanging around or the Sabbat spies (or full blown packs), guests, diplomats, etc etc etc<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the game was never intended to run like that outside really big cities, and I find this cosmopolitan take even worse than the problem of the &quot;100k rule&quot;.<br /> <br /> Kindred do not embrace until they can fill every niche, they create roles as those are needed/useful. Only the Prince is needed, a Sheriff and a Keeper are useful if you can have them, everything else is optional. Primogen in particular are a stupid thing if you don't have a big population, since the 1st edition they're a happenstance, not standard fare to begin with. And simply put, most places don't have every clan, period. Not even every Camarilla clan.<br /> <br /> Again, travelers help here. Not every NPC in a chronicle must live within the area from day 1 to the very end. At any time you feel the need for a member of another clan or an Elder or something to come up, just have them come from the outside.<br /> <br /> It's also hard to justify statistics and at the same time say you can do with more than 1 vampire per 10k inhabitants. If we take your own suggestion of using disappearances as a basis, the average in the US is 6,5 per 100k per year. Well, a vampire that never uses any power consumes a human body worth of Blood every 10 days, so that's 36,5 people per year...<br /> <br /> Of course, there are nuances, but there are nuances for both sides, a lot of them. If we run this realism-like just short of remembering that vampires don't exist, we'll get something very similar to the 100k number, with some wiggle room, sure, but a wiggle room with consequences.<br /> <br /> So you either ignore this number (which is perfectly fine to do), or you don't sweat with having complex vampire societies outside a metropolis, you can't really have a lot of vampires and justify what you do with math.<br /> <br /> For anyone who <b>want</b> to have credible numbers, I'd say: 1:100k is ideal, 1:50k is fine. You can have as much as 1:10k, but then put in the game the signs of the pressure, maybe people are worried about using too much Blood, maybe there are rotations and budgets in place, maybe any small mistake gets hunter attention. More vampires than that, the setting should be somewhat exceptional to justify, but is still doable.<br /> <br /> But again, if you don't want to run a population under pressure, just ignore the numbers altogether and don't think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T03:25:21-07:00","id":1554408,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d bet money that \u2018Primogen\u2019 is a title that has been used to borrow glory nearly as often as it has been used to indicate real distinction: if nothing else it\u2019s safer to claim you\u2019re the senior member of your Clan (Especially when the local representatives of said Clan are all your own brood) than it is to assert Praxis.<br /> <br /> Put another way, it\u2019s a useful title with which to assert seniority and prestige without actually requiring you to hazard all comers by asserting authority over all local vampires (Especially in a more Camarilla-leaning region, where Elders are generally respected, rather than priority targets).<br /> <br /> Heck, I wonder how often titles like \u2018Sheriff\u2019 are used in regions where there\u2019s no Prince, but the locals want some form of Law &amp; Order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T03:29:05-07:00","id":1554409,"title":"","content":"Now that I think on it, I wonder how many would-be Princes in regions where the Kindred tend to be younger have adopted the title \u2018Sheriff\u2019 instead? (Possibly as the thin end of the wedge: start a Sheriff, end a Prince).<br /> <br /> Heck, \u2018Marshal\u2019 could be another usefully-ambiguous title: \u2018Marshal\u2019 as in \u2018Servant of the Court\u2019, as in \u2018The Only Law West of the Pecos\u2019, or as in \u2018Field Marshal\u2019?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T15:40:09-07:00","id":1554452,"title":"","content":"In my games, one player created a really fantastic rule about the Primogen and how they're chosen.<br /> <br /> &quot;To become a Primogen, you have to pass one test and one test alone. You show up at a meeting of the Primogen, sit down, and no one kicks you out.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}